; Imports from kernel32.dll for the SDK-free verification build.
;
; The @N suffixes are the stdcall name decoration on x86 and have to match the
; argument size in bytes. llvm-dlltool is invoked with -k so that the import
; name in the DLL directory carries no suffix - which is how kernel32 actually
; exports these functions.
LIBRARY kernel32.dll
EXPORTS
VirtualProtect@16
VirtualAlloc@16
GetCurrentProcess@0
FlushInstructionCache@12
CreateFileA@28
WriteFile@20
CloseHandle@4
OutputDebugStringA@4
GetPrivateProfileStringA@24
GetModuleFileNameA@12
LoadLibraryA@4
GetProcAddress@8
FreeLibrary@4
GetFileAttributesA@4
